      "writtenOn": "2024-10-28T07:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see.. ok.. Now, it makes sense. \n\n1: With first approach, it may increase the boot time - specifically during shrink\n\n2: Second approach - when the next restart of the app is done, we should make sure that the prior disk resize is fully complete; basically (3) and (4) should be serialized.\n\nI am ok with the first approach if it means to keep it simple.",
      "parentUuid": "9a4554ae_f4e29b68",
      "revId": "592b52a867da765935fb34ed5ae983c7321e6549",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
